# Atlas Database Rules

- Postgres is canonical.
- pgvector is MVP vector search.
- Every memory object needs workspace, owner, visibility, source, status, and timestamps.
- Relation edges must be typed, sourced, confidence-scored, and visibility-filtered.
- Destructive migrations require explicit approval and rollback plan.
- Add indexes for workspace, visibility, type, status, timestamps, full-text, and vector search as needed.
- Do not use JSONB as a lazy replacement for core relational fields.
- Add visibility / single-user scope tests when touching schema or queries. Shared-space leakage tests return when sharing ships (post-MVP).
